			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Resolve naming collisions and stabilize Wasmtime 20 integration\n\nThis commit addresses compilation errors introduced by recent WASM and Spine upgrades by refactoring the module hierarchy and aligning with Wasmtime 20's API changes. The primary goal is to resolve ambiguous import errors (E0255) and ensure type safety across the extension host.\n\n**Naming Convention & Namespace Hygiene:**\n- Introduced the `Impl` suffix for all concrete struct implementations (e.g., `ExtensionHost` -> `ExtensionHostImpl`, `SpineConnection` -> `SpineConnectionImpl`, `Transport` variants -> `...Impl`). This distinguishes implementation types from their defining modules.\n- Moved internal build modules to `*Mod.rs` and made them private, restricting re-exports in `mod.rs` to prevent namespace pollution.\n- Renamed `gRPCTransport` to `GrpcTransport` to adhere to PascalCase acronym standards.\n\n**Wasmtime 20 Compatibility & Fixes:**\n- Updated `WASMRuntime` configuration to match Wasmtime 20.0.2, handling changes to `WasmBacktraceDetails` and WASI setup.\n- Refactored `FunctionExport` to use `wasmparser` types and temporarily disabled complex async closure wrapping to allow compilation while the correct signature for Wasmtime 20 is determined.\n- Fixed `ModuleLoader` generics to use `StoreLimits` explicitly.\n\n**Logic & Borrowing Corrections:**\n- Fixed borrowing issues in `APIBridge` (`from_json_value` clone), `HostBridge` (wrapping `AsyncCallback` sender in `Arc<Mutex>`), and `Activation` (cloning events before moves).\n- Added `Debug` derives to core transport and host structs for better introspection.\n- Added `#[cfg(feature = \"grpc\")]` guards in `Entry` to allow building the host without gRPC dependencies.\n\n**Impact:** The Grove codebase now compiles cleanly with the updated dependency stack. The `Impl` suffix pattern provides a scalable solution for future module additions without risking naming conflicts.",
			"SHA": "78ca1c4ae60d6279395f774958c14756905552ce"
